        "title": "Not for everyone.",
        "text": "Pashupatinath is Nepal’s holiest Hindu Pilgrimage site but we could not go in. But this place was a big surprises for us. Open cremation were done in the just outside of the temple. The river was a small stream but the guide said it is part of Ganges River. \n\nWe also saw few sadhu sitting there and collect few dollars from a tourist who want took a picture with them.\nIt is an experience for us but I will not recommend to every one.\nNon Hindu were not allowed into the temple.\n",
