        "title": "Holy place for Hindus",
        "text": "This temple is primarily for Hindus. \nA visit here may be a bit disturbing for a western tourist as one is greeted by the sight of dead bodies being cremated at the Ghats on the banks of the Bagmati river. This reminds us of the impermanence of life.\nThe Main shrine has a Shivling with four visible faces - 'Tatpurush' faces East, 'Aghor' faces South, 'Sadyojat' faces West, 'Vamadev' faces North, and the fifth face 'Ishana' is supposed to face the Sky. There are 4 entrances to the Main shrine to view each face. \nThe Main shrine is surrounded by smaller shrines.\nTip: The path from the entrance gate to the Ghats is dotted with small shops which sell, among other things, Saligrams. Some of these are Ammonite fossils from the Kali-Gandaki River.",
