        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r261927348-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Looking into life and death in Nepal",
        "text": "Is difficult to say what is most fascinating about this temple, the smells and sounds hit you first - totally alien in the main though the smell of goat brought back a few childhood memories. Troops of monkeys roam the environs of the temple making for the some useful snaps to take back home but unfortunately the temple itself is out of bounds to all but worshipping Hindus. You have to content yourself with the view through the main door from a respectful distance which does give you a glimpse of the massive golden bull, the centrepiece of its central courtyard. Unfortunately perhaps its from the rear end so you are greeted by an infeasibly large pair of golden.. well I'm sure you know water.\n\nRound the back you cross over the holy river and usually an incite into the funeral rites of the Hindu religion. Remember the significance of this place and if you must take pictures take them discretely. Our guide informed us of overenthusiastic tourists who barged mourners out of the way just to get a snap to show off to their friends back home.  The locals were not best pleased.",
        "review_tip": null,
